# The image only needs the application and the files of docker_config/.
*
!rails_app/
!docker_config/
# Development, test and tooling files of the application never reach the image.
rails_app/.bundle
rails_app/.mutant
rails_app/.yardoc
rails_app/coverage
rails_app/doc
rails_app/log/*
rails_app/sorbet
rails_app/spec
rails_app/storage/*
rails_app/tmp/*
# The image configures its database with DATABASE_URL (Dockerfile) instead of config/database.yml, which only
# development and test use; the encrypted credentials are useless without their master key, which is never
# committed (the image generates SECRET_KEY_BASE instead, see docker_config/entrypoint.sh).
rails_app/config/database.yml
rails_app/config/credentials.yml.enc
rails_app/config/master.key
